            "text": "<p><strong>Weight</strong><br>Match weight to the fish and the flies you throw. A 5-weight covers a lot of trout water. Go lighter for small streams and dries. Go heavier for wind, streamers, or larger fish.</p><h3>Freshwater trout</h3><p>Most Ilwaco customers start here. Length and action are preference after weight is right.</p><h3>Salt and bigger flies</h3><p>More backbone, guides that take abuse, and a blank that recovers when the wind is up. Pair with a sealed-drag reel from the <a href=\"/collections/fly-reels\">fly reels</a> aisle.</p><h3>Spey and switch</h3><p>Two-handed tools for bigger water and longer casts. Buy the length and grain window the line calls for, not the longest tube on the wall.</p><h3>Brand aisles</h3><p>Jump into <a href=\"/collections/douglas-outdoors-fly-rods\">Douglas</a>, <a href=\"/collections/echo-fly-rods\">Echo</a>, <a href=\"/collections/g-loomis-fly-rods\">G. Loomis</a>, or <a href=\"/collections/sage-fly-rods\">Sage</a> with the chips, then compare length and weight on each product page.</p>"
